IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `epd-nouns`
IMPORT `epd-seat-sender`

-- CASES for the sender's seat (epd-seat-sender.l4). Every question has at least one case; the expected value of each was decided from
-- the text of the Directive before the run, and the reason is written above the assertion. Every call names its arguments.
-- The mirror cases (the same message put to the recipient's seat) are in epd-cases-seat-mirror.l4.

§ `May I send this message? (Article 13)`
-- S1: May I send this marketing message to this recipient (Art 13)?
-- An e-mail the recipient consented to beforehand, nothing disguised.
#ASSERT (`May I send this marketing message to this recipient` WITH `how I send it` IS `an electronic mail message`, `my message is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `the recipient did not ask for it` IS TRUE, `the recipient is a natural person` IS TRUE, `the recipient consented beforehand` IS TRUE, `I got the recipient's details from the recipient as my customer` IS FALSE, `I got them in the context of a sale` IS TRUE, `I got them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE, `I am the same person that got the details` IS TRUE, `I am marketing my own products or services` IS TRUE, `they are similar to what the recipient bought` IS TRUE, `I clearly and distinctly offered the recipient a way to object` IS TRUE, `the offer to object was free` IS TRUE, `the offer to object was easy` IS TRUE, `I offered it when I collected the details` IS TRUE, `the recipient initially refused such use` IS FALSE, `I offered it with each message` IS TRUE, `my message disguises or conceals who I am` IS FALSE, `my message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS FALSE, `my message has no valid address for requests to stop` IS FALSE, `my message pushes the recipient to a website that breaks that Article` IS FALSE, `national law has chosen` IS `national legislation has not been stated`, `the recipient does not wish to receive these messages` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No consent, but the existing-customer exception is satisfied in every limb.
#ASSERT (`May I send this marketing message to this recipient` WITH `how I send it` IS `an electronic mail message`, `my message is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `the recipient did not ask for it` IS TRUE, `the recipient is a natural person` IS TRUE, `the recipient consented beforehand` IS FALSE, `I got the recipient's details from the recipient as my customer` IS TRUE, `I got them in the context of a sale` IS TRUE, `I got them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE, `I am the same person that got the details` IS TRUE, `I am marketing my own products or services` IS TRUE, `they are similar to what the recipient bought` IS TRUE, `I clearly and distinctly offered the recipient a way to object` IS TRUE, `the offer to object was free` IS TRUE, `the offer to object was easy` IS TRUE, `I offered it when I collected the details` IS TRUE, `the recipient initially refused such use` IS FALSE, `I offered it with each message` IS TRUE, `my message disguises or conceals who I am` IS FALSE, `my message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS FALSE, `my message has no valid address for requests to stop` IS FALSE, `my message pushes the recipient to a website that breaks that Article` IS FALSE, `national law has chosen` IS `national legislation has not been stated`, `the recipient does not wish to receive these messages` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No consent and no exception: paragraph 1 allows it "only" with prior consent.
#ASSERT (`May I send this marketing message to this recipient` WITH `how I send it` IS `an electronic mail message`, `my message is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `the recipient did not ask for it` IS TRUE, `the recipient is a natural person` IS TRUE, `the recipient consented beforehand` IS FALSE, `I got the recipient's details from the recipient as my customer` IS FALSE, `I got them in the context of a sale` IS FALSE, `I got them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS FALSE, `I am the same person that got the details` IS FALSE, `I am marketing my own products or services` IS FALSE, `they are similar to what the recipient bought` IS FALSE, `I clearly and distinctly offered the recipient a way to object` IS FALSE, `the offer to object was free` IS FALSE, `the offer to object was easy` IS FALSE, `I offered it when I collected the details` IS FALSE, `the recipient initially refused such use` IS FALSE, `I offered it with each message` IS FALSE, `my message disguises or conceals who I am` IS FALSE, `my message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS FALSE, `my message has no valid address for requests to stop` IS FALSE, `my message pushes the recipient to a website that breaks that Article` IS FALSE, `national law has chosen` IS `national legislation has not been stated`, `the recipient does not wish to receive these messages` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Paragraph 4 applies in any event: no valid address for requests to stop, even with consent.
#ASSERT (`May I send this marketing message to this recipient` WITH `how I send it` IS `an electronic mail message`, `my message is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `the recipient did not ask for it` IS TRUE, `the recipient is a natural person` IS TRUE, `the recipient consented beforehand` IS TRUE, `I got the recipient's details from the recipient as my customer` IS FALSE, `I got them in the context of a sale` IS FALSE, `I got them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS FALSE, `I am the same person that got the details` IS FALSE, `I am marketing my own products or services` IS FALSE, `they are similar to what the recipient bought` IS FALSE, `I clearly and distinctly offered the recipient a way to object` IS FALSE, `the offer to object was free` IS FALSE, `the offer to object was easy` IS FALSE, `I offered it when I collected the details` IS FALSE, `the recipient initially refused such use` IS FALSE, `I offered it with each message` IS FALSE, `my message disguises or conceals who I am` IS FALSE, `my message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS FALSE, `my message has no valid address for requests to stop` IS TRUE, `my message pushes the recipient to a website that breaks that Article` IS FALSE, `national law has chosen` IS `national legislation has not been stated`, `the recipient does not wish to receive these messages` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A recipient that is a company: paragraph 5 leaves paragraphs 1 and 3 aside, so the text does not answer.
#ASSERT (`May I send this marketing message to this recipient` WITH `how I send it` IS `an electronic mail message`, `my message is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `the recipient did not ask for it` IS TRUE, `the recipient is a natural person` IS FALSE, `the recipient consented beforehand` IS FALSE, `I got the recipient's details from the recipient as my customer` IS FALSE, `I got them in the context of a sale` IS FALSE, `I got them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS FALSE, `I am the same person that got the details` IS FALSE, `I am marketing my own products or services` IS FALSE, `they are similar to what the recipient bought` IS FALSE, `I clearly and distinctly offered the recipient a way to object` IS FALSE, `the offer to object was free` IS FALSE, `the offer to object was easy` IS FALSE, `I offered it when I collected the details` IS FALSE, `the recipient initially refused such use` IS FALSE, `I offered it with each message` IS FALSE, `my message disguises or conceals who I am` IS FALSE, `my message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS FALSE, `my message has no valid address for requests to stop` IS FALSE, `my message pushes the recipient to a website that breaks that Article` IS FALSE, `national law has chosen` IS `national legislation has not been stated`, `the recipient does not wish to receive these messages` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- S2: Has the recipient's prior consent made this use of the means allowed (Art 13(1))?
-- A fax the recipient consented to.
#ASSERT (`Has the recipients prior consent made this use of the means allowed` WITH `how I send it` IS `a facsimile machine`, `my message is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `the recipient consented beforehand` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An automated call the recipient did not consent to: "only in respect of subscribers or users who have given their prior consent".
#ASSERT (`Has the recipients prior consent made this use of the means allowed` WITH `how I send it` IS `an automated calling and communication system without human intervention`, `my message is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `the recipient consented beforehand` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A call with a person is not one of the three means named.
#ASSERT (`Has the recipients prior consent made this use of the means allowed` WITH `how I send it` IS `another means of communication`, `my message is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `the recipient consented beforehand` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- S3: Is this the kind of use Art 13(1) names (Art 13(1))?
-- Electronic mail for direct marketing.
#ASSERT (`Is this the kind of use Article 13(1) names` WITH `how I send it` IS `an electronic mail message`, `my message is for direct marketing` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Electronic mail that is not for direct marketing: silent.
#ASSERT (`Is this the kind of use Article 13(1) names` WITH `how I send it` IS `an electronic mail message`, `my message is for direct marketing` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- S4: Does the existing-customer exception cover this message (Art 13(2))?
-- An e-mail to my own customer about my own similar products, with the chance to object at collection and on each message.
#ASSERT (`Does the existing customer exception cover this message` WITH `how I send it` IS `an electronic mail message`, `I got the recipient's details from the recipient as my customer` IS TRUE, `I got them in the context of a sale` IS TRUE, `I got them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE, `I am the same person that got the details` IS TRUE, `I am marketing my own products or services` IS TRUE, `they are similar to what the recipient bought` IS TRUE, `I clearly and distinctly offered the recipient a way to object` IS TRUE, `the offer to object was free` IS TRUE, `the offer to object was easy` IS TRUE, `I offered it when I collected the details` IS TRUE, `the recipient initially refused such use` IS FALSE, `I offered it with each message` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The chance to object was not offered on each message: a grant whose "provided that" gate failed.
#ASSERT (`Does the existing customer exception cover this message` WITH `how I send it` IS `an electronic mail message`, `I got the recipient's details from the recipient as my customer` IS TRUE, `I got them in the context of a sale` IS TRUE, `I got them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE, `I am the same person that got the details` IS TRUE, `I am marketing my own products or services` IS TRUE, `they are similar to what the recipient bought` IS TRUE, `I clearly and distinctly offered the recipient a way to object` IS TRUE, `the offer to object was free` IS TRUE, `the offer to object was easy` IS TRUE, `I offered it when I collected the details` IS TRUE, `the recipient initially refused such use` IS FALSE, `I offered it with each message` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A fax: the exception is read as covering electronic mail messages only (fork register).
#ASSERT (`Does the existing customer exception cover this message` WITH `how I send it` IS `a facsimile machine`, `I got the recipient's details from the recipient as my customer` IS TRUE, `I got them in the context of a sale` IS TRUE, `I got them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE, `I am the same person that got the details` IS TRUE, `I am marketing my own products or services` IS TRUE, `they are similar to what the recipient bought` IS TRUE, `I clearly and distinctly offered the recipient a way to object` IS TRUE, `the offer to object was free` IS TRUE, `the offer to object was easy` IS TRUE, `I offered it when I collected the details` IS TRUE, `the recipient initially refused such use` IS FALSE, `I offered it with each message` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- S5: May I use this means given the recipient's consent or the existing-customer exception (Art 13(1) and (2))?
-- Consent given.
#ASSERT (`May I use this means given consent or the existing customer exception` WITH `how I send it` IS `an electronic mail message`, `my message is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `the recipient consented beforehand` IS TRUE, `I got the recipient's details from the recipient as my customer` IS FALSE, `I got them in the context of a sale` IS FALSE, `I got them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS FALSE, `I am the same person that got the details` IS FALSE, `I am marketing my own products or services` IS FALSE, `they are similar to what the recipient bought` IS FALSE, `I clearly and distinctly offered the recipient a way to object` IS FALSE, `the offer to object was free` IS FALSE, `the offer to object was easy` IS FALSE, `I offered it when I collected the details` IS FALSE, `the recipient initially refused such use` IS FALSE, `I offered it with each message` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No consent, the exception satisfied.
#ASSERT (`May I use this means given consent or the existing customer exception` WITH `how I send it` IS `an electronic mail message`, `my message is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `the recipient consented beforehand` IS FALSE, `I got the recipient's details from the recipient as my customer` IS TRUE, `I got them in the context of a sale` IS TRUE, `I got them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE, `I am the same person that got the details` IS TRUE, `I am marketing my own products or services` IS TRUE, `they are similar to what the recipient bought` IS TRUE, `I clearly and distinctly offered the recipient a way to object` IS TRUE, `the offer to object was free` IS TRUE, `the offer to object was easy` IS TRUE, `I offered it when I collected the details` IS TRUE, `the recipient initially refused such use` IS FALSE, `I offered it with each message` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No consent and no exception.
#ASSERT (`May I use this means given consent or the existing customer exception` WITH `how I send it` IS `an electronic mail message`, `my message is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `the recipient consented beforehand` IS FALSE, `I got the recipient's details from the recipient as my customer` IS FALSE, `I got them in the context of a sale` IS FALSE, `I got them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS FALSE, `I am the same person that got the details` IS FALSE, `I am marketing my own products or services` IS FALSE, `they are similar to what the recipient bought` IS FALSE, `I clearly and distinctly offered the recipient a way to object` IS FALSE, `the offer to object was free` IS FALSE, `the offer to object was easy` IS FALSE, `I offered it when I collected the details` IS FALSE, `the recipient initially refused such use` IS FALSE, `I offered it with each message` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Other unsolicited marketing, and what is prohibited in any event (Article 13(3) and (4))`
-- S6: Does Art 13(3) apply to this call or message (Art 13(3))?
-- A live marketing call, unsolicited.
#ASSERT (`Does Article 13(3) apply to this call or message` WITH `how I send it` IS `another means of communication`, `the recipient did not ask for it` IS TRUE, `it is for direct marketing` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An e-mail is a case of paragraph 1 or 2, not paragraph 3.
#ASSERT (`Does Article 13(3) apply to this call or message` WITH `how I send it` IS `an electronic mail message`, `the recipient did not ask for it` IS TRUE, `it is for direct marketing` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- S7: Must national law stop this unsolicited call or message (Art 13(3))?
-- A live marketing call where national law requires consent and none was given.
#ASSERT (`Must national law stop this unsolicited call or message` WITH `how I send it` IS `another means of communication`, `the recipient did not ask for it` IS TRUE, `it is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `national law has chosen` IS `consent of the subscriber or user is required`, `the recipient consented` IS FALSE, `the recipient does not wish to receive it` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Where national law protects people who do not wish to receive such calls, and the recipient does not.
#ASSERT (`Must national law stop this unsolicited call or message` WITH `how I send it` IS `another means of communication`, `the recipient did not ask for it` IS TRUE, `it is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `national law has chosen` IS `subscribers or users who do not wish to receive the communications are protected`, `the recipient consented` IS FALSE, `the recipient does not wish to receive it` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- National law's choice is outside the sources, but the recipient gave no consent and does not wish to receive such calls: the option "not allowed without the consent" prohibits it, and so does the option "not allowed in respect of ... users who do not wish to receive these communications", so the text decides it whichever option national law chose (fork F19).
#ASSERT (`Must national law stop this unsolicited call or message` WITH `how I send it` IS `another means of communication`, `the recipient did not ask for it` IS TRUE, `it is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `national law has chosen` IS `national legislation has not been stated`, `the recipient consented` IS FALSE, `the recipient does not wish to receive it` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- National law's choice is outside the sources, and the recipient gave no consent but has not said they do not wish to receive such calls: the first option prohibits it and the second does not, so the text does not decide it (fork F19).
#ASSERT (`Must national law stop this unsolicited call or message` WITH `how I send it` IS `another means of communication`, `the recipient did not ask for it` IS TRUE, `it is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `national law has chosen` IS `national legislation has not been stated`, `the recipient consented` IS FALSE, `the recipient does not wish to receive it` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- National law's choice is outside the sources, and the recipient consented but also does not wish to receive such calls: consent answers the first option and the objection the second, so the text does not decide it (fork F19).
#ASSERT (`Must national law stop this unsolicited call or message` WITH `how I send it` IS `another means of communication`, `the recipient did not ask for it` IS TRUE, `it is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `national law has chosen` IS `national legislation has not been stated`, `the recipient consented` IS TRUE, `the recipient does not wish to receive it` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- S8: Is the option national law chose free of charge for the recipient, as Art 13(3) requires?
-- It is free of charge.
#ASSERT (`Is the national option free of charge for the recipient as Article 13(3) requires` WITH `the option is free of charge for the recipient` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "both options must be free of charge for the subscriber or user".
#ASSERT (`Is the national option free of charge for the recipient as Article 13(3) requires` WITH `the option is free of charge for the recipient` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- S9: Is the practice of sending this e-mail prohibited in any event (Art 13(4))?
-- An e-mail for direct marketing that conceals who sent it: "shall be prohibited".
#ASSERT (`Is the practice of sending this e-mail prohibited in any event` WITH `how I send it` IS `an electronic mail message`, `my message is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `my message disguises or conceals who I am` IS TRUE, `my message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS FALSE, `my message has no valid address for requests to stop` IS FALSE, `my message pushes the recipient to a website that breaks that Article` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An e-mail with none of the four features: the paragraph does not say it is allowed.
#ASSERT (`Is the practice of sending this e-mail prohibited in any event` WITH `how I send it` IS `an electronic mail message`, `my message is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `my message disguises or conceals who I am` IS FALSE, `my message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS FALSE, `my message has no valid address for requests to stop` IS FALSE, `my message pushes the recipient to a website that breaks that Article` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A fax that conceals who sent it: paragraph 4 is about electronic mail.
#ASSERT (`Is the practice of sending this e-mail prohibited in any event` WITH `how I send it` IS `a facsimile machine`, `my message is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `my message disguises or conceals who I am` IS TRUE, `my message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS FALSE, `my message has no valid address for requests to stop` IS FALSE, `my message pushes the recipient to a website that breaks that Article` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- S10: Do paragraphs 1 and 3 apply to this recipient as a natural person (Art 13(5))?
-- Paragraphs 1 and 3 apply to subscribers who are natural persons.
#ASSERT (`Do paragraphs 1 and 3 apply to this recipient as a natural person` WITH `the recipient is a natural person` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a natural person: silent.
#ASSERT (`Do paragraphs 1 and 3 apply to this recipient as a natural person` WITH `the recipient is a natural person` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- S11: The recipient is a company: must its legitimate interests be sufficiently protected (Art 13(5))?
-- A company: Member States shall ensure its legitimate interests are sufficiently protected.
#ASSERT (`The recipient is a company: must its legitimate interests be sufficiently protected` WITH `the recipient is a natural person` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A natural person: the sentence is about other subscribers.
#ASSERT (`The recipient is a company: must its legitimate interests be sufficiently protected` WITH `the recipient is a natural person` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Being taken to court, ordered to stop, or penalised (Articles 13(6), 15, 15a)`
-- S12: May someone bring legal proceedings against me over this message (Art 13(6))?
-- A recipient adversely affected, with a legitimate interest.
#ASSERT (`May someone bring legal proceedings against me over this message` WITH `the person is adversely affected by the infringement` IS TRUE, `the person has a legitimate interest in stopping it` IS TRUE, `the person is an electronic communications service provider protecting its business interests` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A provider adversely affected and protecting its legitimate business interests.
#ASSERT (`May someone bring legal proceedings against me over this message` WITH `the person is adversely affected by the infringement` IS TRUE, `the person has a legitimate interest in stopping it` IS FALSE, `the person is an electronic communications service provider protecting its business interests` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not adversely affected: a power whose gate failed.
#ASSERT (`May someone bring legal proceedings against me over this message` WITH `the person is adversely affected by the infringement` IS FALSE, `the person has a legitimate interest in stopping it` IS TRUE, `the person is an electronic communications service provider protecting its business interests` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- S13: If someone sues me, can the authority still act against me administratively (Art 13(6))?
-- "Without prejudice to any administrative remedy": legal proceedings leave it unaffected.
#ASSERT (`If someone sues me can the authority still act against me administratively` WITH `national law provides an administrative remedy under Art 15a(2)` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No administrative remedy: silent.
#ASSERT (`If someone sues me can the authority still act against me administratively` WITH `national law provides an administrative remedy under Art 15a(2)` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- S14: Must my Member State have penalties for this infringement (Art 15a(1))?
-- Member States shall lay down the rules on penalties applicable to infringements.
#ASSERT (`Must my Member State have penalties for this infringement` WITH `it is an infringement of the national rules under this Directive` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not such an infringement: silent.
#ASSERT (`Must my Member State have penalties for this infringement` WITH `it is an infringement of the national rules under this Directive` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- S15: May a penalty cover the whole period of a breach I have since put right (Art 15a(1))?
-- "may be applied to cover the period of any breach, even where the breach has subsequently been rectified".
#ASSERT (`May a penalty cover the whole period of a breach I have since put right` WITH `the penalty is applied to cover the period of the breach` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A penalty that does not cover the period: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`May a penalty cover the whole period of a breach I have since put right` WITH `the penalty is applied to cover the period of the breach` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- S16: Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to order me to stop (Art 15a(2))?
-- The competent national authority must have the power to order the cessation of the infringement.
#ASSERT (`Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to order me to stop` WITH `it is an infringement of the national rules under this Directive` IS TRUE, `the body is the competent national authority` IS TRUE, `the body is another national body` IS FALSE, `it is relevant for that body to have the power` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Another national body for which it is not relevant: "where relevant".
#ASSERT (`Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to order me to stop` WITH `it is an infringement of the national rules under this Directive` IS TRUE, `the body is the competent national authority` IS FALSE, `the body is another national body` IS TRUE, `it is relevant for that body to have the power` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not an infringement of the national provisions: silent.
#ASSERT (`Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to order me to stop` WITH `it is an infringement of the national rules under this Directive` IS FALSE, `the body is the competent national authority` IS TRUE, `the body is another national body` IS FALSE, `it is relevant for that body to have the power` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- S17: Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to require me, as a sender, to give it information when it investigates (Art 15a(3))?
-- The competent national authority must have the power to obtain any relevant information.
#ASSERT (`Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to require me as a sender to give it information when it investigates` WITH `the body is the competent national authority` IS TRUE, `the body is another national body` IS FALSE, `it is relevant for that body to have the powers` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A body that is neither: silent.
#ASSERT (`Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to require me as a sender to give it information when it investigates` WITH `the body is the competent national authority` IS FALSE, `the body is another national body` IS FALSE, `it is relevant for that body to have the powers` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- S18: Do the judicial remedies and sanctions of Directive 95/46/EC apply against me (Art 15(2))?
-- National provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive: Chapter III applies.
#ASSERT (`Do the judicial remedies and sanctions of Directive 95 46 EC apply against me` WITH `it concerns national provisions adopted under this Directive` IS TRUE, `it concerns an individual right derived from this Directive` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither: silent.
#ASSERT (`Do the judicial remedies and sanctions of Directive 95 46 EC apply against me` WITH `it concerns national provisions adopted under this Directive` IS FALSE, `it concerns an individual right derived from this Directive` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Is it electronic mail, is it consent, and what I put on the recipient's device (Articles 2 and 5)`
-- S19: Is my message "electronic mail" under the Directive (Art 2(h))?
-- A text message sent over a public network and stored until collected: electronic mail.
#ASSERT (`Is my message electronic mail under the Directive` WITH `it is a text, voice, sound or image message` IS TRUE, `I send it over a public communications network` IS TRUE, `it can be stored until the recipient collects it` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A live call that cannot be stored: not electronic mail.
#ASSERT (`Is my message electronic mail under the Directive` WITH `it is a text, voice, sound or image message` IS TRUE, `I send it over a public communications network` IS TRUE, `it can be stored until the recipient collects it` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- S20: Is what the recipient did "consent" under the Directive (Art 2(f))?
-- The borrowed requirement is met.
#ASSERT (`Is what the recipient did consent under the Directive` WITH `what the recipient did is consent in the sense of Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not met: not consent.
#ASSERT (`Is what the recipient did consent under the Directive` WITH `what the recipient did is consent in the sense of Directive 95/46/EC` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- S21: Do I need consent to store information on the recipient's device or read it (Art 5(3))?
-- "only allowed on condition that the subscriber or user concerned has given his or her consent".
#ASSERT (`Do I need consent to store information on the recipients device or read it` WITH `I store information on the recipient's device or read what is on it` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No storage or access: silent.
#ASSERT (`Do I need consent to store information on the recipients device or read it` WITH `I store information on the recipient's device or read what is on it` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- S22: Have I met the condition of consent for what I store on, or read from, the recipient's device (Art 5(3))?
-- Consent, clear information, Directive 95/46/EC met.
#ASSERT (`Have I met the condition of consent for what I store on or read from the recipients device` WITH `the recipient gave consent` IS TRUE, `I gave clear and comprehensive information` IS TRUE, `the consent and information meet Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No clear and comprehensive information.
#ASSERT (`Have I met the condition of consent for what I store on or read from the recipients device` WITH `the recipient gave consent` IS TRUE, `I gave clear and comprehensive information` IS FALSE, `the consent and information meet Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

